yes,  you'll just use an optimized orthogonal rotation criterion - like varimax - to rotate the draws and then resolve permutations in the manner we show in the paper.   the whole thing is much simpler than the alternatives i'd initially considered.  the real reason to dispense with the loadings restrictions is because it removes dependence on ordering of variables (unlike for MLE), rather than implementation in STAN, but you'll achieve better mixing - particularly if you use parameter expansion - and once you set up the two post-processing steps, you'll be able to easily do this in any future models you'd conceive.

