>>>> parameters before and after a latent temporal change point.
>>>>
>>>> The simple case I’ll use for illustration is univariate linear
>>>> regression of response variable y as a function of predictor x, which is a
>>>> random variable drawn once per time step from a normal distribution N(.) .
>>>> There is also a Gaussian noise term in the response, with standard deviation
>>>> sig_y.
>>>>
