>
> > Thanks Bob. Perhaps I've mixed up two points. First, Stan would be better than nuts n bolts in R, given points about continuous parameters etc. No point debating that in this forum. Second, I feel that journal readers are poorly served by pages of algebra and no straightforward BUGS/Stan code. With good checking, it should be ok to present a new model in this way. After all, I don't have to write down the likelihood and Newton-Raphson every time I publish a logistic regression.
